sem_post clears a semaphore's waiters bit when it wakes the waiters.
The bit, set by a thread before it sleeps in sem_wait, stayed set for
good once any thread had slept: every later sem_post made a futex wake
system call though no one waited, and sem_trywait failed with EAGAIN
whatever the count was, as it takes the bit to mean that the count is
taken. sem_post now gives the new count without the bit and wakes every
waiter if the bit was set, as it already woke them all; each one that
then finds nothing to take sets the bit again before it sleeps. A
thread that set the bit slept while the word held the value from before
it did, which no longer matched, so its first wait returned at once and
took a second system call; it now sleeps while the word holds the bit.
Meant for upstream.

--- a/options/posix/generic/semaphore.cpp
+++ b/options/posix/generic/semaphore.cpp
@@ -40,7 +40,9 @@
 		if (!(state & semaphoreCountMask)) {
 			if (__atomic_compare_exchange_n(&sem->__mlibc_count, &state, semaphoreHasWaiters,
 						false, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE)) {
-				int e = mlibc::thread_cancellable_futex_wait((int *)&sem->__mlibc_count, state, nullptr);
+				// Sleeps while the word holds what was just stored there.
+				int e = mlibc::thread_cancellable_futex_wait((int *)&sem->__mlibc_count,
+						semaphoreHasWaiters, nullptr);
 				if (e == 0 || e == EAGAIN) {
 					continue;
 				} else if (e == ECANCELED) {
@@ -94,7 +96,8 @@
 					return -1;
 				}
 
-				int e = mlibc::thread_cancellable_futex_wait((int *)&sem->__mlibc_count, state, &timeout);
+				int e = mlibc::thread_cancellable_futex_wait((int *)&sem->__mlibc_count,
+						semaphoreHasWaiters, &timeout);
 
 				if (e == 0 || e == EAGAIN) {
 					continue;
@@ -130,7 +133,11 @@
 			return -1;
 		}
 
-		auto new_state = (count + 1) | (state & semaphoreHasWaiters);
+		// The waiters, if any, are all woken below, so the bit goes: each
+		// that finds nothing to take sets it again before it sleeps. A
+		// post with no one asleep then makes no system call, and a count
+		// above zero never has the bit.
+		auto new_state = count + 1;
 
 		if (__atomic_compare_exchange_n(&sem->__mlibc_count, &state, new_state, true, __ATOMIC_RELEASE, __ATOMIC_RELAXED))
 			break;
